---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "What grammar mistakes lower IELTS writing scores most often?",
    answer:
      "Common score-lowering mistakes include subject-verb agreement problems, double subjects, and unnatural word order in sentences that try to sound too formal.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can a few grammar mistakes really affect my score?",
    answer:
      "Yes. A few repeated grammar mistakes can make the whole response feel less controlled, especially when the same error appears again and again.",
  },
  {
    question: "How can I reduce grammar mistakes faster?",
    answer:
      "Focus on a few repeated error patterns, write slowly enough to stay in control, and check the same problem areas every time you review your work.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "Grammar Mistakes in IELTS", path: "/blog/grammar-mistakes-ielts/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="Grammar Mistakes That Lower IELTS Scores | Fix the Most Common Ones First"
  description="A practical guide to the grammar mistakes IELTS students repeat most often, with simpler fixes that improve control quickly."
  type="article"
  keywords="IELTS grammar mistakes, IELTS writing grammar errors, subject verb agreement IELTS"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section guide-article">
    <a class="guide-back-link" href="/blog">Back to blog</a>

    <header class="guide-header">
      <span class="guide-tag">IELTS grammar guide</span>
      <h1 style="margin: 0;">Grammar mistakes that lower IELTS scores</h1>
      <div class="guide-meta">
        <span>March 17, 2026</span>
        <span>6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-lead">
      <p>
        Most students do not lose grammar marks because of rare advanced structures. They
        lose marks because a few common mistakes keep repeating. If you fix those patterns,
        your writing and speaking start to feel much more controlled.
      </p>
      <p>
        The fastest improvement usually comes from noticing what you do again and again.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="guide-card">
      <h2>Three mistakes that appear again and again</h2>
      <div class="guide-steps">
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Subject-verb agreement with long subjects</h3>
            <p>Students follow the nearest noun instead of the real subject.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Double subjects</h3>
            <p>The noun is repeated with a pronoun, which makes the sentence ungrammatical.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Risky word order</h3>
            <p>Writers try to sound formal, but the sentence order becomes unnatural.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Examples of safer corrections</h2>
      <table class="guide-mistake-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Weak sentence</th>
          <th>Better sentence</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The number of students who study abroad are increasing.</td>
          <td>The number of students who study abroad is increasing.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>My sister, she lives in Calgary.</td>
          <td>My sister lives in Calgary.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Under no circumstances I will accept this.</td>
          <td>I will not accept this under any circumstances.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Why these mistakes happen</h2>
      <div class="guide-grid guide-grid-2">
        <div class="guide-note">
          <p>
            Some errors come from translation. The sentence pattern feels normal in another
            language, so it slips into English.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-note">
          <p>
            Other errors happen because students try to sound more advanced before the basic
            sentence is stable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>A better checking habit</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>Find the real subject before you check the verb.</li>
        <li>Make sure one clause has one clear subject.</li>
        <li>Keep word order simple unless you are fully sure the advanced pattern is correct.</li>
        <li>Check your last three sentences before you submit, not only the first paragraph.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>Next step</h2>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="/lessons/grammar/subject-verb-agreement/">
          <strong>Study subject-verb agreement</strong>
          <span>Fix one of the most common grammar patterns first.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/lessons/grammar">
          <strong>Browse grammar lessons</strong>
          <span>Open the full grammar lesson library.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/tutoring">
          <strong>Get direct feedback</strong>
          <span>Use tutoring if you want someone to catch your repeated error patterns.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <div class="guide-faq">
        {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="card">
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <section class="section-sm" style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center;">
    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin-bottom: var(--s-5);" />
    <p class="muted">Want a CLB 9 writing system you can actually follow?</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/celpip/writing">Get the system</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
